= Future Work <FutureWork>
The results showed that retaining Jython support is no longer beneficial and introduces unnecessary maintenance complexity into `pygrametl`. Dropping Jython support would eliminate the need to maintain several Jython-specific components, including the `JDBCConnectionWrapper` for `java.sql` connections, `jythonmultiprocessing`, and `sys.platform.startswith("java")` guards and Jython-specific compatibility workarounds across `parallel.py`, `datasources.py`, and `tables.py`. Furthermore, focusing development exclusively on modern CPython would make it easier to adopt newer Python features for performance gains, such as free-threading, without having to account for compatibility with an older runtime. It could also simplify future development and maintenance while allowing `pygrametl` to benefit more readily from continued improvements to the Python ecosystem.